== impute: IterativeImputer (one round recomputed with exact OLS)
ok   IterativeImputer(max_iter=0): result = the initial (mean) imputation, n_iter_ = 0
ok   IterativeImputer(max_iter=0, initial_strategy='median') = SimpleImputer(median)
   missing counts per column: [2, 2, 1]
ok   IterativeImputer(LinearRegression, max_iter=1, imputation_order='roman'): visiting order [0, 1, 2] (left to right) and one round = exact OLS chained imputation (rel 1e-8)  (sequence [0, 1, 2], max diff 8.9e-16)
ok   IterativeImputer(LinearRegression, max_iter=1, imputation_order='arabic'): visiting order [2, 1, 0] (right to left) and one round = exact OLS chained imputation (rel 1e-8)  (sequence [2, 1, 0], max diff 1.8e-15)
ok   IterativeImputer(LinearRegression, max_iter=1, imputation_order='ascending'): visiting order [2, 0, 1] (fewest missing first (counts 2,2,1; tie in stable order)) and one round = exact OLS chained imputation (rel 1e-8)  (sequence [2, 0, 1], max diff 1.8e-15)
ok   IterativeImputer(LinearRegression, max_iter=1, imputation_order='descending'): visiting order [1, 0, 2] (most missing first (reverse of ascending)) and one round = exact OLS chained imputation (rel 1e-8)  (sequence [1, 0, 2], max diff 1.8e-15)
ok   IterativeImputer imputation_order 'ascending' = 'From features with fewest missing values to most' [1, 2, 0]; 'descending' = [0, 2, 1] (ties keep / reverse the stable order)  ([1, 2, 0], [0, 2, 1])
ok   IterativeImputer(descending) one round = OLS chained imputation in the order [0, 2, 1] (rel 1e-8)
ok   IterativeImputer(imputation_order='random'): 'A random order for each round' -> each round is a permutation of the features; deterministic with random_state  ([2, 0, 1, 0, 2, 1, 2, 0, 1])
ok   IterativeImputer(skip_complete=True): complete feature 1 not in imputation_sequence_ (n_features_with_missing_ = 2); skip_complete=False fits it anyway; identical imputations
ok   IterativeImputer(skip_complete=True).transform: a feature complete at fit but missing at transform 'will be imputed with the initial imputation method only' (mean of column 1)  (3.0 vs mean 3.0)
ok   IterativeImputer(max_iter=2, tol=0): two rounds = two passes of the exact chained OLS (rel 1e-8), n_iter_ = 2
   clipping: unclipped imputed values [2.3398, 1.6018, 6.5268, 0.511, 5.5914] -> clipped [2.8069, 2.0, 6.0, 2.0, 4.0]
ok   IterativeImputer(min_value=2, max_value=[inf, 4, 6]): imputed values clipped per feature inside the chain (exact chained OLS with clipping, rel 1e-8); clipping changes at least one value here
ok   IterativeImputer(tol=0.1): stops at the first round t with max|X_t - X_(t-1)|/max|X[known]| < tol (documented criterion) -> n_iter_ = 2  (n_iter_ 2; changes/scale ['7.3e-02', '2.4e-02'])
ok   IterativeImputer(tol=0.01): stops at the first round t with max|X_t - X_(t-1)|/max|X[known]| < tol (documented criterion) -> n_iter_ = 4  (n_iter_ 4; changes/scale ['7.3e-02', '2.4e-02', '8.0e-03', '3.2e-03'])
ok   IterativeImputer(tol=0.001): stops at the first round t with max|X_t - X_(t-1)|/max|X[known]| < tol (documented criterion) -> n_iter_ = 7  (n_iter_ 7; changes/scale ['7.3e-02', '2.4e-02', '8.0e-03', '3.2e-03', '1.4e-03', '6.7e-04', '3.1e-04'])
ok   IterativeImputer(tol=0.0001): stops at the first round t with max|X_t - X_(t-1)|/max|X[known]| < tol (documented criterion) -> n_iter_ = 8  (n_iter_ 8; changes/scale ['7.3e-02', '2.4e-02', '8.0e-03', '3.2e-03', '1.4e-03', '6.7e-04', '3.1e-04'])
ok   IterativeImputer that does not converge within max_iter warns (ConvergenceWarning)
ok   IterativeImputer(sample_posterior=True): deterministic given random_state, different seeds differ, 'early stopping is only applied if sample_posterior=False' -> n_iter_ = max_iter
ok   IterativeImputer with a single feature: initial imputation returned, n_iter_ = 0
ok   IterativeImputer(add_indicator=True): imputed columns then indicator columns
ok   IterativeImputer with an all-missing feature: dropped by default, kept as 0 with keep_empty_features=True
== compose: ColumnTransformer / TransformedTargetRegressor
ok   ColumnTransformer(remainder='drop'): output = [transformer 1 output | transformer 2 output] in transformers order ('The order of the columns ... follows the order of how the columns are specified'), unspecified columns dropped
ok   ColumnTransformer(remainder='passthrough'): remaining columns (2, 4) appended after the transformers, in their original order ('This subset of columns is concatenated with the output of the transformers')
ok   ColumnTransformer(remainder=estimator): remaining columns transformed by the remainder estimator, appended last
ok   ColumnTransformer column selection by slice / boolean mask / callable(X) -> same as index lists
ok   ColumnTransformer(transformer_weights): 'The output of the transformer is multiplied by these weights'
ok   ColumnTransformer.fit_transform = fit then transform
ok   ColumnTransformer.named_transformers_ holds the fitted transformers (StandardScaler mean_ of columns 0, 1)
ok   ColumnTransformer.get_feature_names_out(verbose_feature_names_out=True): 'sc__a', 'sc__b', 'mm__d'; passthrough remainder -> 'remainder__c', 'remainder__e'  (['mm__d', 'sc__a', 'sc__b', 'remainder__c', 'remainder__e'])
ok   ColumnTransformer(verbose_feature_names_out=False): plain input names
ok   ColumnTransformer(verbose_feature_names_out=False) with duplicate output names raises ValueError ('will error if feature names are not unique')
ok   ColumnTransformer(sparse_threshold=0.3): overall density 0.4 (nnz 16 / 40) >= threshold -> dense ('stacked as a sparse matrix if the overall density is lower than this value'; 0 -> always dense)  (sparse=False)
ok   ColumnTransformer(sparse_threshold=0.5): overall density 0.4 (nnz 16 / 40) < threshold -> sparse ('stacked as a sparse matrix if the overall density is lower than this value'; 0 -> always dense)  (sparse=True)
ok   ColumnTransformer(sparse_threshold=0.0): overall density 0.4 (nnz 16 / 40) >= threshold -> dense ('stacked as a sparse matrix if the overall density is lower than this value'; 0 -> always dense)  (sparse=False)
ok   ColumnTransformer(sparse_threshold=1.0): overall density 0.4 (nnz 16 / 40) < threshold -> sparse ('stacked as a sparse matrix if the overall density is lower than this value'; 0 -> always dense)  (sparse=True)
ok   ColumnTransformer with all-dense outputs stays dense whatever the threshold ('this keyword will be ignored')
ok   make_column_transformer names transformers by lowercased class name ('standardscaler', 'minmaxscaler')
ok   ColumnTransformer with string column names on a numpy array raises ValueError ('Specifying the columns using strings is only supported for dataframes')
   (column selection by name / make_column_selector(dtype_include) / set_output('pandas') need pandas, not installed: skipped)
ok   ColumnTransformer with 'drop' and 'passthrough' as transformers: dropped column absent, passthrough column verbatim
ok   TransformedTargetRegressor(func=log, inverse_func=exp): regressor_ fitted on func(y) (exact OLS on log y, rel 1e-12)
ok   TransformedTargetRegressor.predict = inverse_func(regressor_.predict(X)) exactly (exp of the linear prediction), 1-d output
ok   TransformedTargetRegressor(transformer=StandardScaler): regressor_ fitted on transformer.transform(y) (2-d internally), predict = transformer_.inverse_transform(regressor_.predict(X)) (rel 1e-12)
ok   TransformedTargetRegressor with a linear regressor and StandardScaler on y predicts exactly like plain LinearRegression (affine invariance)
ok   TransformedTargetRegressor(check_inverse=True) with non-inverse func pair: UserWarning 'The provided functions or transformer are not strictly inverse of each other'
ok   TransformedTargetRegressor(check_inverse=False): no warning
ok   TransformedTargetRegressor default (no func/transformer): identity -> predictions equal LinearRegression
ok   TransformedTargetRegressor(func without inverse_func) raises ValueError
ok   TransformedTargetRegressor(transformer and func both set) raises ValueError
ok   TransformedTargetRegressor.score = r2 of the back-transformed predictions (r2_exact)
== pipeline: Pipeline / FeatureUnion / make_pipeline / make_union
ok   Pipeline.fit chains fit_transform: intermediate steps equal manual chaining (scaler mean_, PCA components_ up to sign, classifier coef_)
ok   Pipeline[:-1].transform(X) = manual chained transform (PCA sign fixed by comparing |.|); pipe[:-1] is a Pipeline of the first steps
ok   Pipeline.predict_proba / decision_function / predict = the final estimator applied to the transformed X (passthrough)
ok   Pipeline steps slicing: pipe[0] is the StandardScaler, pipe[-1] the classifier, pipe['pca'] by name, pipe[1:] a Pipeline of pca+clf
ok   Pipeline.score(X, y, sample_weight) = final_estimator.score(Xt, y, sample_weight) (weighted accuracy, exact)
ok   Pipeline with 'passthrough' and None steps: they are skipped (classifier fitted on the raw X)
ok   Pipeline.set_params with nested 'step__param' names reaches the step parameters
ok   Pipeline.set_params(step=new_estimator) replaces the step
ok   Pipeline(memory=joblib.Memory): the second fit with identical data and params reuses the cached transformer (fit not called again) and gives identical results to the uncached pipeline  (fit calls after 1st/2nd cached fit: 1, 1)
ok   Pipeline(memory) with a string path also works
ok   Pipeline.get_feature_names_out chains the steps' feature names (scaler one-to-one -> pca0, pca1)
ok   Pipeline.fit_transform on a transformer-only pipeline = chained fit_transform (exact)
ok   Pipeline.inverse_transform applies the steps' inverse_transform in reverse
ok   Pipeline with a non-transformer intermediate step raises TypeError
ok   make_pipeline names steps by lowercased class name, duplicates suffixed -1, -2: ['standardscaler-1','standardscaler-2','pca','logisticregression']  (['standardscaler-1', 'standardscaler-2', 'pca', 'logisticregression'])
ok   FeatureUnion: outputs concatenated horizontally in transformer order (2 + 4 + 14 columns; PCA compared up to sign)
ok   FeatureUnion(transformer_weights): 'Multiplicative weights for features per transformer'
ok   FeatureUnion.get_feature_names_out prefixes with the transformer name ('sc__x0', ...)  (['pca__pca0', 'pca__pca1', 'sc__x0'])
ok   FeatureUnion with 'drop' and 'passthrough' transformers: dropped one contributes nothing, passthrough gives X verbatim
ok   make_union names transformers by lowercased class name with -1/-2 suffixes for duplicates  (['standardscaler-1', 'minmaxscaler', 'standardscaler-2'])
ok   FeatureUnion with one sparse output returns a sparse matrix with dense blocks stacked
ok   FeatureUnion.fit_transform = fit + transform
== done
